# Rank 1346 / CVE-2017-12629: the CVE bundles two unrelated Solr issues under
# one id -- an RCE through the RunExecutableListener reachable from the config
# API, and an XXE in the XML query parser. Pool commit d8000beebf (SOLR-11477,
# "Disallow resolving of external entities in Lucene queryparser/xml/CoreParser
# and SolrCoreParser") is the *XXE* half, and that is the half this spec
# encodes; the RunExecutableListener half is a different commit and a different
# weakness class (CWE-502/CWE-78), not this one (CWE-611).
#
# Step 0, `repo!` flag: the advisory names `apache/lucene` while the pool row
# says `apache/lucene-solr`. This is a split artefact, not a dependency
# mislink. `apache/lucene-solr` was the combined Lucene+Solr repository, later
# split into `apache/lucene` and `apache/solr`, and `apache/lucene` kept the
# full pre-split history: `gh api repos/apache/lucene-solr/commits/d8000beebf`
# and `gh api repos/apache/lucene/commits/d8000beebf` both resolve to the same
# object, d8000beebfb13ba0b6e754f84c760e11592d8d14. The pool row is the better
# scan target of the two, because the fix touches
# `solr/core/src/java/org/apache/solr/search/SolrCoreParser.java` as well as
# `lucene/queryparser/.../CoreParser.java`, and the `solr/` tree exists only in
# `lucene-solr` -- it moved to `apache/solr` at the split, so a scan of
# `apache/lucene` can never see half of this fix. No pool row replacement.
#
# `CoreParser.parseXML` built a stock JAXP DocumentBuilder and parsed the
# caller's stream with it:
#
#   private static Document parseXML(InputStream pXmlFile) throws ParserException {
#     DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
#     DocumentBuilder db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
#     return db.parse(pXmlFile);
#   }
#
# A default DocumentBuilderFactory resolves DOCTYPE-declared external entities
# and external DTDs. Solr's `SolrCoreParser` extends `CoreParser`, and
# `defType=xmlparser` / `{!xmlparser ...}` routes the request's own query
# string into `parse()`, so a query carrying
# `<!DOCTYPE x [<!ENTITY e SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd">]>` makes the server
# read local files and fetch attacker-chosen URLs -- CWE-611.
#
# The fix hardens the factory before building (`dbf.setValidating(false)` plus
# `dbf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true)`) and installs
# an overridable `EntityResolver` on the builder that throws on any external
# entity (`DISALLOW_EXTERNAL_ENTITY_RESOLVER`); `SolrCoreParser` additionally
# overrides `getErrorHandler()` to route parse warnings to Solr's log.
#
# CAUGHT by VYQL-DESER-004 (code.XmlParserCreate, medium/high-confidence), and
# this rank separates the revisions on the real checkout. Scanning
# `lucene/queryparser` plus `SolrCoreParser.java` at d8000beebf^ reports 12
# findings including `code.XmlParserCreate @ CoreParser.java:137` -- the CVE's
# own `dbf.newDocumentBuilder()` line -- with both
# `unless endpoint coveredBy core.XmlHardening` and
# `unless sameReceiver coveredBy core.XmlHardening` unsatisfied. At d8000beebf
# that row is gone: binding xmlHardening272 matches `setFeature` with an
# argument naming FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING and covers `sameReceiver` anchored
# on the callee's receiver, which the fix supplies on the same `dbf` local.
#
# Note which control gets the credit, because it is not the one the advisory
# talks about. `db.setEntityResolver(getEntityResolver())` is this fix's actual
# XXE defence, and it has no binding in any language: `setEntityResolver` is
# ambiguous from the JAXP documentation alone -- a resolver can just as easily
# be installed to *enable* custom entity fetching as to refuse it, so binding
# it to core.XmlHardening would fail the genericity test. The suppression here
# rides entirely on the incidental FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING call, and it also
# sits on the wrong object for `sameReceiver` anyway (the builder `db`, not the
# factory `dbf`).
#
# The same scan pair exposed a second thing, unrelated to this CVE and pinned
# by the last two cases below: `sameReceiver` coverage is matched on the
# receiver's *identifier text*, scan-wide, with no file or scope qualification.
# `Engine.sameReceiverGuardReceivers` (internal/engine/engine.go:1295) folds
# every guard node carrying a concrete `sameReceiver` coverage into one
# `map[receiverName]bool` cached per control, and `Engine.sameReceiverGuarded`
# (engine.go:1245) consults it by name whenever the sink's own `recv` node
# carries no coverage. So one hardening call on a local named `dbf` suppresses
# every `code.XmlParserCreate` whose receiver is also named `dbf`, anywhere in
# the scan. That is why the fixed revision reports 7 rather than the 11 the
# CVE line's removal alone would leave: `DOMUtils.java:195`,
# `QueryTemplateManager.java:148`, `:173` and `:197` are byte-identical between
# the two revisions and each calls `dbf.newDocumentBuilder()` on an unhardened
# factory, yet all four go quiet the moment the fixed `CoreParser` hardens its
# own `dbf`. Confirmed minimal: two classes in separate packages and separate
# directories, one hardening a `dbf` and one not, report nothing; renaming the
# unhardened local restores the finding. Scoping the name fallback is not a
# mechanical correction -- the map is deliberately unscoped so a factory
# hardened in an initialiser and used in another method still counts, several
# languages share the mechanism through core.XmlHardening and every other
# `same_receiver_guard` control, and narrowing it trades recall for precision
# on every one of them. Entered in ENGINE-GAPS.md rather than attempted here.
#
# verify_current_expected: caught, both real revisions separated
#
# Spec only; no definition change. OWASP Java and Python unchanged at +1.00
# and +0.90.

test "rank1346: CoreParser.parseXML builds a DocumentBuilder from an unhardened factory"
  lang java
  file lucene/queryparser/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queryparser/xml/CoreParser.java
  expect VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.lucene.queryparser.xml;

  import java.io.InputStream;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
  import org.w3c.dom.Document;

  public class CoreParser {

    private static Document parseXML(InputStream pXmlFile) throws ParserException {
      DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      DocumentBuilder db = null;
      try {
        db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
      }
      catch (Exception se) {
        throw new ParserException("XML Parser configuration error", se);
      }
      org.w3c.dom.Document doc = null;
      try {
        doc = db.parse(pXmlFile);
      }
      catch (Exception se) {
        throw new ParserException("Error parsing XML stream:" + se, se);
      }
      return doc;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1346: the fix hardens the factory and refuses external entities on the builder"
  lang java
  file lucene/queryparser/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queryparser/xml/CoreParser.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.lucene.queryparser.xml;

  import java.io.IOException;
  import java.io.InputStream;
  import java.util.Locale;
  import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
  import javax.xml.parsers.ParserConfigurationException;
  import org.w3c.dom.Document;
  import org.xml.sax.EntityResolver;
  import org.xml.sax.ErrorHandler;
  import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
  import org.xml.sax.SAXException;

  public class CoreParser {

    protected EntityResolver getEntityResolver() {
      return DISALLOW_EXTERNAL_ENTITY_RESOLVER;
    }

    protected ErrorHandler getErrorHandler() {
      return null;
    }

    private Document parseXML(InputStream pXmlFile) throws ParserException {
      final DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      dbf.setValidating(false);
      try {
        dbf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
      } catch (ParserConfigurationException e) {
      }
      final DocumentBuilder db;
      try {
        db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
      } catch (Exception se) {
        throw new ParserException("XML Parser configuration error.", se);
      }
      try {
        db.setEntityResolver(getEntityResolver());
        db.setErrorHandler(getErrorHandler());
        return db.parse(pXmlFile);
      } catch (Exception se) {
        throw new ParserException("Error parsing XML stream: " + se, se);
      }
    }

    public static final EntityResolver DISALLOW_EXTERNAL_ENTITY_RESOLVER =
        new EntityResolver() {
          @Override
          public InputSource resolveEntity(String publicId, String systemId) throws SAXException, IOException {
            throw new SAXException(String.format(Locale.ENGLISH,
                "External Entity resolving unsupported:  publicId=\"%s\" systemId=\"%s\"",
                publicId, systemId));
          }
        };
  }
  ```

test "rank1346: a hardened factory suppresses an unrelated unhardened one that happens to share its local's name"
  lang java
  file lucene/queryparser/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queryparser/xml/DOMUtils.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.lucene.queryparser.xml;

  import java.io.InputStream;
  import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
  import org.w3c.dom.Document;

  public class DOMUtils {

    public static Document parseHardened(InputStream is) throws Exception {
      DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      dbf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
      DocumentBuilder db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
      return db.parse(is);
    }

    public static Document loadXML(InputStream is) throws Exception {
      DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      DocumentBuilder db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
      return db.parse(is);
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1346: renaming the unhardened factory's local, and nothing else, restores the finding"
  lang java
  file lucene/queryparser/src/java/org/apache/lucene/queryparser/xml/DOMUtils.java
  expect VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.lucene.queryparser.xml;

  import java.io.InputStream;
  import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
  import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
  import org.w3c.dom.Document;

  public class DOMUtils {

    public static Document parseHardened(InputStream is) throws Exception {
      DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      dbf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
      DocumentBuilder db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
      return db.parse(is);
    }

    public static Document loadXML(InputStream is) throws Exception {
      DocumentBuilderFactory plainFactory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      DocumentBuilder db = plainFactory.newDocumentBuilder();
      return db.parse(is);
    }
  }
  ```
